{
  "example": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.agent_config`\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.with_agent`\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.validation-cache.with_agent`\n\nThis Bedrock configuration selects a model, AWS profile, and region for the\ndomain's cache:\n\n```rust,ignore\nuse trust_but_verify::agent::AgentConfig;\nuse trust_but_verify::agent::BedrockConfig;\nuse trust_but_verify::domain::ValidationCache;\n\nlet config = AgentConfig::Bedrock(\n    BedrockConfig::new(\"us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5\".into())\n        .aws_profile(\"development\".into())\n        .region(\"us-east-1\".into()),\n);\nlet cache = ValidationCache::<AppDomain>::with_agent(config);\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The example `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.setup` gives a concrete case. A Bedrock `AgentConfig` with the model `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5`, the profile `development` and the region `us-east-1` is passed to `ValidationCache::with_agent`. Its cited requirements say the cache is created empty, requests through the cache and its clones use that agent, backend setup is deferred, and the SDK does not persist the configuration.\n\n`crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bedrock_configuration_attaches_to_a_cache_without_being_persisted]` carries a `{test}` reference to `setup`. It builds the same Bedrock config with the same three values and calls `ValidationCache::with_agent(config.clone())`. Its assertions check each outcome:\n- **Selection:** `cache().agent.backend == config` shows the model, profile and region were selected for the cache.\n- **Empty cache:** `outlines` is empty and `sources` is `None`.\n- **Clones share the agent:** `Arc::ptr_eq` on the agent of the domain and its clone `peer` shows this.\n- **Not persisted:** the test runs `refresh_evidence` on `Question(false, ...)`, which is a criterion that doesn't ask the agent. It then serializes the saved record. The record has no `backend` key and doesn't contain `development` or `claude-sonnet`.\n- **Deferred setup:** the same `refresh_evidence` call succeeds with the Bedrock config and never awaits an agent request. That is consistent with backend setup being deferred. It is a weaker check than the others.\n\nThe `TestDomain` and `Question` helpers support these assertions. I found no unresolved gap.",
  "references": "7c7524ee8e51af918c33943dcb55e9936d8e326b278323071bdbeabdfe57c6a0",
